lena-cs: Heads up - FastStart (trial customer) reporting intermittent 429s during SDK bootstrap on embedded webviews. QA is blocked for their demo tomorrow. Can we triage?

sam-eng: Can you paste the logs? Is it during cold start or after long idle?

lena-cs: Customer says its most reproducible when they open multiple tabs/app windows at once (kiosk mode). Logs: 
```
[2026-03-23T08:02:11Z] event=client.init org=fs-42 status=200
[2026-03-23T08:02:11Z] event=client.init org=fs-42 status=429 msg="preflight-rate"
[2026-03-23T08:02:11Z] event=serviceworker.sync org=fs-42 status=200
[2026-03-23T08:02:12Z] event=client.init org=fs-42 status=429 msg="token_refresh_rate"
```
They mentioned some windows call init from both the main frame and an embedded worker.

toni-ops: Sounds like a thundering herd at preflight/token refresh layer. Our charts show short bursts for org fs-42 at 08:02 ~900rpm in a 60s slice. We have two fast options: server-side debounce/coalesce and client backoff/dedupe.

sam-eng: For immediate relief we can enable per-org request coalescing and increase their short-window throttle threshold temporarily. For a better SDK solution: use BroadcastChannel or localStorage "init-lock" to coordinate across tabs/webviews and a singleflight on init Promise. Example pattern: 
```js
// cross-tab singleflight
const bc = new BroadcastChannel('redwood-init');
let initPromise;
bc.onmessage = (m) => { if (m.data === 'init-start') { /* wait */ } }
function init() {
  if (initPromise) return initPromise;
  bc.postMessage('init-start');
  initPromise = fetch('/v1/preflight').finally(() => { initPromise = null; bc.postMessage('init-done'); });
  return initPromise;
}
```
This helps in multi-tab kiosks. Also add jittered retry on 429.

lena-cs: Customer can't modify kiosk app before demo. They asked for a temporary server-side fix.

toni-ops: I can flip a coalesce flag for org fs-42 and raise their per-minute burst by +400 for 6 hours. We also support honoring an idempotency header `x-client-debounce-key`—if the SDK can send a consistent key per logical session the gateway will collapse duplicates. We can document that for them post-demo.

infra-bot: action: enable-coalesce(org=fs-42) -> success; burst-increase org=fs-42 +400 (expires 6h).

redwood-ratebot: alert: preflight spike fs-42 900rpm -> coalesce enabled; burst cap increased. Monitoring for 15m.

lena-cs: Please confirm TTL behavior for ephemeral tokens while coalescing is on. Customer worried refresh windows.

toni-ops: While coalescing, we extended ephemeral token TTL from 18s -> 40s for that org to reduce refresh frequency. We'll revert after 6h.

sam-eng: Follow-ups: 1) PR to SDK: cross-tab BroadcastChannel singleflight + capped concurrent preflights (max 2) + jittered backoff on 429s. 2) Docs page: "Integrating in multi-tab or embedded WebView environments". 3) Gateway: add short doc for `x-client-debounce-key`.

lena-cs: I told FastStart we're applying the temporary change and will run the demo. They appreciate the fast turnaround. I'll schedule a 30m follow-up next week to help them adopt the SDK patch. Thank you everyone :heart:
